{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1154114-stranger-things-season-two","id":1154114,"title":"Stranger Things Season Two","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-30T06:39:03-07:00","id":1154114,"title":"Stranger Things Season Two","content":"Anyone else binge watch this one yet? I mean...I loved season one, beyond belief, even made my wife who despises horror/sci-fi/etc. watch it in entirety over the weekend and follow up with a season 2 binge session (all 9 hours or so). I have to say, I'm completely blown out of the water by it. The way they handled certain things were amazing and I was worried that they would take it a different direction and ruin what they built with season 1, but dayaaaaamn, they most certainly did not!<br /> <br /> I have to say that this also is a good show to take from for CofD (certain games of course) chronicles and plots seeds and so on. Of course I am (obviously) a serious fanboy of this series lol.<br /> <br /> What were your thoughts (if you saw it thus far).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T12:20:43-07:00","id":1154180,"title":"","content":"Just finished it last night. It was amazing. I had only two very minor nitpicks related to editing choices.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">In Hop\u2019s shack in the woods where eleven is staying, we see a shot of him carefully stepping over the trip wire. That\u2019s a set-up shot. Later, we see him rigging the trip wire up to fire the warning shot in a flashback. That\u2019s a reminder. Clearly the show wants us to remember that this trip wire exists and will play an important role. Later still, when eleven is consciously breaking all of the Don\u2019t Be Stupid rules, we see her carefully step over the trip wire. That\u2019s a second reminder, which is usually an indication that the payoff is coming soon. But it never comes. Right up to the last episode I was speculating how that trip wire was going to pay off. As soon as the Mind Flayer heard the phone ring and they had to change hiding spots, I correctly predicted that they would go to the shack in the woods, and noted that Hop gave them directions but did not tell them to watch our for the trip wire. I was sure one of them was going to step on it and the gunshot would attract the attention of the Demogogs, but it never happened. The trip wire never went anywhere.<br /> <br /> Similarly, when Sean Austin\u2019s character reset the lockdown in the lab, they made a point of showing that he left his gun on the table. I correctly predicted that he would get killed after that, but I assumed he would reach for his gun and realize he had left it behind before the demogogog jumped on him. But that didn\u2019t happen. So when Hop and Eleven when back to the lab to close the gate, I thought they\u2019d get cornered and the gun being there would be the thing that saved them. That didn\u2019t happen either. This one doesn\u2019t bother me quite as much as the trip wire because it didn\u2019t have a reminder shot, let alone two reminder shots, but it was still a very clear and intentional setup with no payoff.<br /> <br /> I wonder if either of them had payoffs in earlier cuts that just didn\u2019t make it into the final.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T05:03:24-07:00","id":1154341,"title":"","content":"Excellent points! Here's my take on them:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Your point on the Tripwire is definitely seen. The way I looked at it though was that the whole issue of pointing it out multiple times was that it was used as a barrier for 0011. She eventually crosses over that tripwire stating &quot;not stupid&quot; and this is a huge moment for her because it's her crossing over that line and becoming her own individual. Hence, in my opinion, the &quot;not stupid&quot; being monumental and pointing out that she is no longer a child (remember just prior to this they had the fight where he said &quot;if you want to go out in the world you must grow up!&quot;). We then of course have the side story episode which features 0011 finding her mother and her &quot;sister&quot; and these add to her character's development and 'growing up'. That's my take on that tripwire anyways. I do agree though that Hopper never mentioning the tripwire and no one setting it off was SURELY a oversight on the director/writers/etc.<br /> <br /> The gun missing did not bother me as much in a similar fashion but I think they lost a great opportunity. When he dropped/knocked over the mop, I really thought he would reach to his side or hold up his hand pointed out and realize &quot;oh no&quot; but that never happened.<br /> <br /> All in all, they did an amazing job of representing cosmic fear and showing us how small we actually are because there was NO way they could have faced off with the &quot;shadow demon&quot; of that magnitude so they did what they had to to close the gate...of course this leaves an opening for a Season 3 considering that the parallel world, the &quot;upside down&quot;, is still there...there's just no gate in Hawkins at this point...<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":12143,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","user":"EldritchMinister","date":". 10-31-2017, 08:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}